[02:23:18] Story complete. Summary:
[02:23:18] **What changed** — a synchronization panel in the existing Vue frontend; **no Java file was touched**, so no backend contract or JavaFX workflow changed.
[02:23:18] | File | Role |
[02:23:18] |---|---|
[02:23:18] | `frontend/src/api/syncApi.ts` | the three triggers + shared status route behind an interface |
[02:23:18] | `frontend/src/sync/operations.ts` | the four backend operation keys and their trigger calls |
[02:23:18] | `frontend/src/sync/useSyncOperations.ts` | per-operation submission and bounded status polling |
[02:23:18] | `frontend/src/sync/SyncControls.vue` | one trigger and one task state per operation |
[02:23:18] | `frontend/scripts/sync-browser-smoke.mjs` | real-browser check against a controlled API boundary |
[02:23:18] Plus edits to `api/types.ts`, `api/http.ts` (`API_BASE_PATH` exported), `App.vue`, `package.json`, and `resolveBrowserPath` extracted from the existing smoke script so both browser checks share one lookup list.
[02:23:18] **Key behaviour** — 202 is acceptance only; the four states are read from the status body's `state`, never from the HTTP status. Duplicate clicks are suppressed *per operation*, mirroring the backend's per-key admission rule (a 409 is shown honestly, never resubmitted). Submission errors, task failures and lookup failures are three distinct notices; a transport-failed trigger says the admission is unknown, and a 404 `TASK_NOT_FOUND` reports an outcome that cannot be established — explicitly not success, failure or rollback — with no retry, while other lookup failures offer a retry of the lookup alone. Polling is chained (never overlapping), bounded at 3 s × 600, stopped on terminal/failure/bound, token-guarded against stale answers, and cancelled on unmount.
[02:23:18] **Verification run**
[02:23:18] - `npm run type-check`: clean · `npm test`: **49/49** (26 pre-existing + 23 new) · `npm run build`: OK (81.20 kB JS)
[02:23:18] - `npm run smoke:sync`: **PASSED, 8 steps** in real Chrome — nothing requested on load, four triggers with the documented bodies, buttons disabled while unfinished, a task tracked to `SUCCEEDED`, a `FAILED` task rendered from an HTTP **200**, the two price variants kept apart, polling stopped, no non-backend calls
[02:23:18] - `./mvnw test`: exit 0, **286 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors** (53 report files from this run)
[02:23:18] **Limits I want stated plainly:** no real synchronization was run — the browser check deliberately uses a stub origin, since clicking these buttons live would spend GW2 API budget and write to your database. `smoke:browser` (real backend) was not re-run, only its import path re-verified. The 409 path has controlled-response coverage only. Task records stay process-local, so a reload or restart forgets a tracked task, and a `SUCCEEDED` price refresh establishes no item count. No §33 performance claim, no Phase 5 exit criterion and no milestone transition declared.
[02:23:18] Docs updated: `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` §5.11, `TEST_STRATEGY.md` §12.2/new §12.3, `README.md`; story file, BACKLOG entry and `CLAUDE_RESULT.md` carry the full result. Nothing was committed.
