[11:52:54] ## What I found
[11:52:54] The interrupted attempt had finished the implementation and the documentation, stopping just before the story's `Status` field was set. So the correct action was to **verify rather than rebuild** — and I re-ran everything rather than trusting the recorded claims.
[11:52:54] ## What was already delivered
[11:52:54] - **Shell** (`frontend/src/shell/`) — `destinations.ts` (four implemented destinations, no dead entries), `useHashRoute.ts` (real URLs, Back/Forward, per-page document titles, no router dependency), `SiteHeader.vue`, `PageHeader.vue`. `App.vue` is the shell: skip link, header, `<main>`.
[11:52:54] - **Shared presentation** (`styles.css`) — tokens, spacing/type scales, and reusable panel/notice/status/table-region treatments replacing every hardcoded hex and opacity-as-hierarchy.
[11:52:54] - **Synchronization as its own area** — `sync/SyncScreen.vue`, with tracking state owned by the shell (`provideSyncOperations.ts`) so an unfinished task survives navigation with no duplicated trigger or second polling loop; `statusPresentation.ts` supplies user-oriented wording.
[11:52:54] ## Verification (all re-run this session)
[11:52:54] | Check | Result |
[11:52:54] |---|---|
[11:52:54] | `npm test` | 98/98, 11 files |
[11:52:54] | `type-check` / `build` | clean; byte-identical sizes to those recorded |
[11:52:54] | `smoke:layout` | PASSED, 11 steps |
