[11:52:54] | `smoke:account` (live, read-only) | PASSED, 8 steps |
[11:52:54] | `smoke:browser` (live, read-only) | PASSED, 8 steps |
[11:52:54] Every figure reproduced exactly — 1547px of columns confined to a 334px region, lowest contrast 4.92:1, 3175 rows, 180 bank slots/17 empty, 9 categories/505 stacks. No file under `src/`, and no `pom.xml`, was touched, so no domain, HTTP contract or JavaFX behavior changed.
[11:52:54] ## Two things worth flagging
[11:52:54] **A cleanup trap I hit.** `TaskStop` killed the `npx` wrapper but the Vite server kept serving. I checked with `netstat`, which reported no listener — but `netstat` returns **zero** LISTENING rows at all in this sandbox, so its silence was a broken tool, not a clean port. Had I trusted it, I'd have left a dev server proxying to your live backend running indefinitely. I identified the process by command line instead, stopped only my two PIDs, and confirmed release by probing. Your four pre-existing `npm run dev` servers are untouched. I recorded this in `tasks/lessons.md`.
[11:52:54] **Limitations carried forward, not resolved:** no screen-reader run and no WCAG conformance claim; contrast measured on selected pairs only; text zoom checked rather than true browser page zoom; the synchronization page has still never been driven against the live backend, so failure and unknown-outcome paths remain controlled-response evidence only. Crafting Profit's columns and its now-non-sticky header are STORY-WEB-005's scope. No §33 performance, Phase 5 exit criterion, or milestone transition is claimed.
