[12:50:18] STORY-WEB-005 is complete and marked DONE.
[12:50:18] ## What changed
[12:50:18] **Crafting Profit is now three groups** — calculation controls, a comparison table, and a separately labelled selected-result detail — side by side from 64rem (shared `.results-split`, detail bounded 20–26rem) and stacked below that width.
[12:50:18] - **Table: 14 columns → 6.** Recipe (a `<th scope="row">`), Disciplines, Craftable, Profit *per craft*, Total profit *all crafts*, State. Each money header states its basis, because the contract genuinely mixes them: `buyCostCopper` and `totalProfitCopper` are totals for every craft counted while `revenueCopper`/`matsSellValueCopper`/`profitCopper` are per single craft (`web.dto.CraftingRowDto`) — the old table placed "Buy cost" among per-craft columns unlabelled.
[12:50:18] - **Nothing dropped from the client.** New `SelectedResultDetail.vue` holds the per-craft group, the totals group, the output quote, a *Crafting steps* region, and **both** material lists — including `missingToBuyOne`, which was never rendered before, and the full `missingToBuy` list, which the table used to truncate to three items. No shopping total, no derived procurement quantity.
[12:50:18] - **Selection is the recipe id, never the row.** The detail is derived from the current rows, so sorting/searching keep it, a replacement calculation refreshes it, a removed recipe clears it, and a superseded response — which never reaches `rows` — can never reach it. The control is an ordinary `<button>` carrying the recipe name; the selection is marked by `aria-current`, a surface, a border, a glyph and a hidden "Selected".
[12:50:18] - **Domain states read as words** (`rowState.ts`), with the raw code only in a closed disclosure; an unrecognized code is shown as itself and never toned as success. Signed money (`+`/`-`) so gain and loss are not told apart by color, with `0c` and `—` both neutral and distinct.
[12:50:18] ## Verification
[12:50:18] `npm test` **132/132** (was 98) · type-check clean · build OK · new `npm run smoke:profit` **PASSED, 12 steps** (side-by-side 968/416px at 1440×900; Enter selected a row with focus kept and visible; selection survived re-sorting; detail below results at 360×800 with no page-level horizontal scrolling) · `smoke:layout` **PASSED, 11 steps**, 21 rendered contrast pairs meet AA (lowest 4.92:1) · `smoke:sync` **PASSED, 9 steps** · live read-only `smoke:browser` **PASSED, 9 steps** (3175 rows, first total `+26g 41s 76c`, detail opened with no further backend request) · live `smoke:account` **PASSED, 8 steps**. No file under `src/` or `pom.xml` was touched, so the Java suite was deliberately not re-run.
[12:50:18] Two things worth flagging: **the resolution tree is not delivered** — the Crafting steps region truthfully states its own absence, and `STORY-APP-012` plus a §13 detail route must land before a frontend story can fill it — and **sorting by buy cost, revenue, mats value, output count and min rating is gone** with those columns, deliberately; the values remain per recipe in the detail. Both, along with the one-tab-stop-per-row cost across 3175 unvirtualized rows and the contrast/zoom measurement limits, are recorded in the story Result. No §33 performance result, Phase 5 exit criterion or milestone transition is claimed.
