[13:27:12] p.write_text('''# ADR-003 - Separate requested recipe identity from actual root sourcing
[13:27:12] ## Status
[13:27:12] ACCEPTED - 2026-09-25. Class C: architecturally significant technical decision.
[13:27:12] Requires Product Owner decision: NO.
[13:27:12] ## Context
[13:27:12] AR-003 exposes an ambiguity in the detail contract established by ADR-002:
[13:27:12] requested recipe identity and actual producing recipe identity need not coincide.
[13:27:12] CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE section 5.12 and STORY-DOM-020's Result document that the
[13:27:12] existing explanation preserves both identities. KNOWN_PROBLEMS CH-15 documents
[13:27:12] finished stock or another recipe satisfying the requested output. DOMAIN_SPEC
[13:27:12] section 28 still defines craftable count as executions of the requested recipe;
[13:27:12] section 44 requires explanations of actual calculation choices.
[13:27:12] ## Constraints
[13:27:12] Preserve authoritative domain evaluation, captured request-local inputs, truthful
[13:27:12] quantities and costs, table compatibility and JavaFX coexistence. A transport
[13:27:12] mapper cannot correct domain economics or manufacture an executed recipe.
[13:27:12] Existing behavior is evidence of a defect, not authority to redefine product intent.
[13:27:12] ## Decision
[13:27:12] Separate selection identity from sourcing identity, and describe the tree as one
[13:27:12] output requirement rather than promising execution of the requested recipe.
[13:27:12] TARGET_ARCHITECTURE sections 13.3-13.5 own the exact revised wire semantics,
[13:27:12] browser obligations and migration constraints; they supersede ADR-002's earlier
[13:27:12] single-craft wording on this point. Other ADR-002 decisions remain in force.
[13:27:12] CH-15 correction is not an architectural prerequisite for delivering a truthful
[13:27:12] explanation of current calculation results. It remains domain debt under its
[13:27:12] existing owner, with no change to the normative definition of craftable count.
[13:27:12] ## Rationale
[13:27:12] Architectural judgment: separate identities faithfully expose facts already
[13:27:12] available from the domain and preserve the incremental migration boundary.
[13:27:12] Changing the basis literal before the documented HTTP/browser integration avoids
[13:27:12] teaching consumers that supplied output proves execution. No dependency, process,
[13:27:12] retained state or additional calculation engine is needed. The contract remains
[13:27:12] useful after a domain correction because selection and actual sourcing are
[13:27:12] separate responsibilities even when their recipe IDs coincide.
[13:27:12] This resolves a representation conflict without deciding new product behavior.
[13:27:12] The intended execution rule is already established by DOMAIN_SPEC section 28;
[13:27:12] this decision neither reverses it nor marks the current calculation compliant.
[13:27:12] ## Alternatives Considered
[13:27:12] - **Require CH-15 correction before detail (runner-up):** aligns current results
[13:27:12]   with intended requested-recipe execution sooner, but couples an explanation
[13:27:12]   integration to a change in shared simulation economics. A truthful detail
[13:27:12]   contract does not technically require that dependency. The planner retains
[13:27:12]   responsibility for defect work and applicable completion gates.
[13:27:12] - **Retain SINGLE_CRAFT with a qualified description:** minimizes a prospective
[13:27:12]   enum change but leaves a misleading execution claim in the machine contract.
[13:27:12]   The documented detail routes and browser integration do not yet exist, so a
[13:27:12]   precise basis now has less compatibility cost than later reinterpretation.
[13:27:12] - **Force requested identity in mapping or reconstruct its ingredients:** rejected
[13:27:12]   because it would misrepresent sourcing, quantities and costs and create a second
[13:27:12]   calculation authority. Hiding valid traces when identities differ likewise
[13:27:12]   conceals the behavior users need explained.
[13:27:12] ## Consequences
[13:27:12] Consumers must distinguish requested selection from actual root sourcing. Detail
[13:27:12] can reveal a known defect in the row calculation; it must not claim to fix it.
[13:27:12] No table shape or JavaFX call boundary changes. The planner owns bounded API/browser
[13:27:12] integration, verification of differing identities and separate disposition of
[13:27:12] CH-15. No milestone acceptance, runtime validation or performance result is claimed.
[13:27:12] ## References
[13:27:12] - [Target architecture](../../TARGET_ARCHITECTURE.md), sections 13.2-13.5.
[13:27:12] - [Current architecture](../../CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md), section 5.12.
[13:27:12] - [Domain specification](../../DOMAIN_SPEC.md), sections 28 and 44.
[13:27:12] - [Known problems](../../KNOWN_PROBLEMS.md), CH-15.
[13:27:12] - [Original contract rationale](ADR-002-resolution-tree-http-contract.md).
[13:27:12] - [Trace result](../../../agent/stories/STORY-DOM-020-semantic-resolution-trace.md).
[13:27:12] - [Dispatched request](../../../agent/architect-requests/AR-003-resolution-root-identity.md).
[13:27:12] ''', encoding='utf-8', newline='')
