[17:08:47] - `CraftingDiscoveryService.resolveDetail(recipeId, choice, settings, inventoryCharacterName)` — individual path, keeping Discovery's separate nullable inventory character and its unfiltered-pool fallback
[17:08:47] Each service's `reload(...)` was split into `loadCandidates(choice)` (visible set, graph recipes, allowed IDs) and `loadCalculationInputs(...)` (quotes, item metadata, roster/inventory pools), extracted verbatim so `reload(...)`'s statement order, Discovery's "no missing recipes" short-circuit and its `lastAllowedRecipeIds`-before-inventory write are all preserved. `resolveDetail` runs those same two steps into request-local records and never touches the `last*` fields — a recipe outside the candidate set returns `RECIPE_NOT_IN_CALCULATION` before any price, item or inventory load.
[17:08:47] **Row and tree from the same captured facts:** the row comes from new `CraftingPlanner.evaluateOne(...)`/`evaluateOneCoordinated(...)` — the table calculation restricted to one recipe (same context, same fresh `PlanState`, same `evaluateOneRecipeNew` including its heuristic skip), the tree from `SingleCraftExplainer` called with the same `CalculationInputs` value. Because each builds its own `PlanState` from the captured initial maps, the row's multi-craft simulation can't become the explanation's starting state.
[17:08:47] New `application.CraftingResolutionDetail` carries calculation facts only; `Status` is derived in its factories, and item names come only from that operation's captured metadata (missing → absent, never `"Item <id>"`).
