[20:06:57] write(p,s[:start]+\"### Item and recipe icon delivery\\n\\n**DECIDED (AR-005, Class C).** Use browser HTTP caching over a backend-owned\\npersistent filesystem cache, with ArenaNet image retrieval only on local miss.\\nThis implements Request-005''s revised requirement and replaces the AR-004\\ndirect-browser contract. It applies to Crafting Profit, Bank, Materials,\\nrecipe/detail trees and future item views. This is target intent, not implemented\\nbehavior. [ADR-005](architecture/decisions/ADR-005-persistent-web-icon-cache.md)\\nrecords the rationale; ADR-004 is superseded. API-009 and WEB-010 still require\\nplanner rescoping before selection. Phase 5 performance and health-review gates\\nremain unchanged.\\n\\n**Canonical metadata and ownership.** Backend synchronization owns GW2 item\\nmetadata; reuse persisted "'`items.icon_url` as the canonical upstream source.'"\\nDo not create another web metadata store. Synchronization must cover referenced\\naccount items, recipe outputs and ingredients, including nontradeable items,\\nand refresh changed URLs during explicit metadata refresh. The existing\\nnull-only URL backfill alone does not satisfy coverage or refresh. Missing\\nmetadata is tolerated and repaired by synchronization, never by page navigation\\nor an image request. Metadata synchronization remains usable without downloading\\nbinaries or running desktop setup; no new browser sync control is required.\\n\\nApplication read services batch-enrich presentation data from retained metadata,\\noutside crafting calculations, with nullable "'`iconUrl`. Recipes use their'"\\nbackend-known output item; detail nodes use their actual item identity.\\nUnsupported/non-item nodes and missing or rejected metadata yield null.\\nNo per-row database lookup, GW2 metadata lookup or image download belongs in\\npage-data reads/calculations. A local metadata read on an image cache miss is\\npermitted; it must never trigger GW2 JSON acquisition. URL parsing, disk and\\nHTTP concerns remain outside the domain. An application icon-delivery boundary\\ncoordinates filesystem and upstream HTTP adapters; HTTP controllers stay thin.\\n\\n**Application URL and source validation.** Emit the application-relative path\\n"'`/api/items/{itemId}/icon/{sourceKey}.{ext}`, served by backend `GET`, as'"\\n"'`iconUrl`. The frontend uses this value verbatim through the application'"''s\\nexisting API routing; development routing must send this path to the backend.\\nNever emit an upstream URL or filesystem "'`iconPath` in browser item contracts.'"\\nMigrate the affected transport types and consumers together; JavaFX may retain\\nlocal paths. No direct ArenaNet image fallback or redirect is allowed.\\n\\nThe source must parse as absolute HTTPS on exactly "'`render.guildwars2.com`,'"\\nwith path "'`/file/{signature}/{file_id}.{ext}`: hexadecimal signature, positive'"\\ndecimal file ID, and lowercase "'`png` or `jpg` extension. Reject userinfo,'"\\nports other than the default HTTPS port, queries, fragments, encoded path\\nseparators, dot segments, other paths, hosts and schemes. Canonicalize scheme\\nand host to lowercase and omit explicit port 443; retain accepted path spelling.\\n"'`sourceKey` is the lowercase 64-hex SHA-256 of that canonical URL'"''s UTF-8 bytes,\\nnot the item ID or a hash of a local path. Centralize this policy in the backend.\\n\\nValidate route item ID, key and extension before any file access. On a local\\nmiss, load that item''s retained source, validate it and require its derived key\\nand extension to match the request before fetching. Unknown items, missing\\nmetadata, and obsolete or mismatched keys return 404 without upstream access.\\nA cached old key may still be served: it identifies an earlier image, never the\\nnew image. Accept no caller-supplied URL, path or host. Disable upstream\\nredirect following; send no API key, cookies, application authorization or\\naccount data upstream. This is an asset endpoint, not an arbitrary proxy.\\nBrowser GW2 API calls remain forbidden.\\n\\n**Persistent storage and hits.** Reuse the configured "'`ICON_CACHE_DIR` root'"\\n(existing local default: "'`<user.home>/.nebet-gw2-tool/icons`).'"\\nThe backend infrastructure adapter owns\\n"'`<ICON_CACHE_DIR>/assets-v1/{sourceKey}.{ext}`. Items sharing the same canonical'"\\nURL share one binary. Only committed, validated image files are cache entries;\\nzero-length, partial or corrupt files are misses and must not be served.\\nConstrain resolved paths to the configured cache root, including symlink\\nhandling; do not expose a directory listing or a generic filesystem route.\\n\\nServe valid hits directly, even during an upstream outage, without external\\nrequests, upstream revalidation or dependence on a live metadata lookup.\\nThere is no backend age-based expiry or routine redownload of successful\\nentries. Browser expiry does not expire the disk copy. A changed retained URL\\nnaturally yields a new key and browser URL on the next application read.\\n\\n**Misses and failures.** For an eligible miss, retrieve only the validated\\ncanonical image URL. Require HTTP 200 and a complete, nonempty, decodable PNG\\nor JPEG matching the extension; reject HTML/error bodies and unsupported types.\\nEnforce finite connection/response deadlines, response-byte and decoded-pixel\\nlimits, and a bounded number of concurrent downloads and waiting requests.\\nThe implementation must choose and document these bounds; they are protective\\nlimits, not a claim about measured latency. Coalesce concurrent requests for\\nthe same key within the backend process and recheck disk after acquiring the\\nkey''s coordination slot. Do not add a distributed locking service.\\n\\nWrite to a unique temporary file in the destination directory, validate and\\natomically publish the complete file before returning success. All writers\\nmust use this publication protocol; readers must never see partial bytes.\\nPersistence failure returns an unavailable response, not a successful\\nuncached image stream. A concurrent publisher must not overwrite an already\\ncommitted valid entry. No background bulk warmup is required.\\n\\nMalformed route values return 400; absent/rejected metadata or upstream 404\\nreturns 404; transient upstream failures, invalid image bodies, exhausted\\ncapacity and disk failures return 503. Every non-success response uses\\n"'`Cache-Control: no-store`; 503 includes a finite `Retry-After`. Do not persist'"\\nfailure bodies or placeholders at image keys. Use bounded, short-lived\\nin-process failure suppression by key to avoid repeated upstream attempts\\nduring an outage; it must expire and must not hide an existing valid disk hit.\\nThere is no persistent negative cache or automatic request retry loop.\\nLog diagnosable failures without secrets or exposing paths to the browser.\\n\\n**Browser caching and rendering.** Successful images use\\n"'`Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400`, the verified `Content-Type`,'"\\n"'`X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, and a strong ETag derived from stored bytes.'"\\nSupport "'`If-None-Match`/304 using the local copy, retaining Cache-Control and'"\\nETag on 304. Use neither an upstream-derived TTL nor "'`immutable`: the one-day'"\\nfreshness interval is an application choice, and permits local repair to become\\nvisible after browser revalidation. Browser eviction/reload can still issue\\nrequests, which use the disk cache. Never substitute different-version bytes\\nunder an old key. No timestamp cache busting, base64 embedding, blob-fetch\\nlayer, service worker or IndexedDB store is needed.\\n\\nShare one frontend image component. Use ordinary images, reserved dimensions,\\nprompt loading of visible images and native offscreen lazy loading where\\nappropriate. Set "'`referrerpolicy='"\\\"no-referrer\\\""'`; if CSP exists, application'"\\nimage delivery needs no ArenaNet origin allowance. On null, rejected URL or\\nload/decode failure, show one bundled neutral placeholder with no upstream\\nfallback or retry loop. Reset failure state on identity/URL change. Retain item\\ntext (backend name or item ID), quantities, rarity, domain states and keyboard\\ninteraction; avoid redundant accessible announcements. Empty bank slots remain\\nempty. Icon failures cannot affect crafting eligibility or result availability.\\n\\n**JavaFX coexistence and existing files.** Keep "'`ICON_CACHE_DIR` and'"\\n"'`items.icon_path` compatibility, but route future `IconSync` binary writes and'"\\nweb misses through the same cache adapter/key/publication policy. Existing\\nexplicit desktop bulk sync remains callable; web use does not require it.\\nJavaFX can consume the shared file via "'`icon_path`, updated only after file'"\\npublication and only while the item''s retained source still matches.\\nA failure to update the desktop path does not invalidate a committed asset.\\nDesktop and backend processes need the same root mounted at usable paths to\\nshare bytes; host-specific absolute database paths are not portable web inputs.\\n\\nLegacy "'`items/{itemId}.png` files are migration candidates, not automatically'"\\ntrusted versioned entries. Observed "'`IconSync` writes no source-version'"\\nprovenance and uses a .png filename even for a source ending in .jpg.\\nValidate actual bytes and require evidence associating them with the current\\ncanonical URL before adoption (recorded provenance, or byte equality with a\\nsuccessful on-demand fetch of that source). Current database URL plus filename\\nalone does not prove that association. With evidence, adopt into the shared\\nkeyed cache using a safe link/copy and update the desktop path; without evidence,\\nleave the legacy file usable by JavaFX and populate the new entry on demand.\\nNo mass redownload or startup migration is required. Remove a legacy copy only\\nafter successful adoption/path migration and confirmation that no retained\\ndesktop reference needs it. Temporary migration copies are acceptable; do not\\nmaintain independent desktop and web download stores going forward.\\n\\n**Retention and deployment.** Retain successful keyed files across backend\\nrestarts, upgrades and container replacement. Container deployment must mount\\na writable persistent volume or host directory at "'`ICON_CACHE_DIR`; an image'"\\nlayer, ephemeral writable layer or temporary directory is insufficient.\\nThe frontend needs no filesystem mount. Use the same configured root across\\nrestarts and diagnose missing/unwritable storage; never silently downgrade to\\nmemory-only delivery. This specifies persistence for existing deployment work,\\nnot a new service/container, deployment story or multi-replica requirement.\\nNo database binary store, distributed cache or external cache service is selected.\\n\\nDo not schedule age-based eviction, TTL refresh or sweeping of valid images.\\nCleanup may remove abandoned temporary files, corrupt entries and safely\\nunreferenced legacy duplicates, with active writers/readers protected.\\nUnreferenced old source keys may remain; no measured storage pressure justifies\\na garbage collector now. Manual removal of a corrupt keyed entry permits\\non-demand repair. Disk-full failures must preserve existing hits and surface\\nas bounded failures on misses. A later retention policy needs evidence and\\nmust preserve Request-005''s normal persistent reuse.\\n\\n**Verification and planner follow-up.** Rescope API-009 and WEB-010 against this\\ncontract before selection; their old direct-CDN/no-cache criteria are obsolete.\\nImplementation evidence must cover URL/null mapping, actual item identities,\\nbatch enrichment, source/route rejection, path confinement, no credentials or\\nfilesystem paths on the wire, and no external calls on page-data reads.\\nVerify local hits with upstream disabled, a successful miss persisted before\\nresponse, same-key concurrent misses, interrupted writes/restart reuse, changed\\nmetadata, invalid/oversized images, upstream and disk failure, bounded recovery,\\nHTTP headers/304, safe legacy reuse and JavaFX compatibility. Use disposable\\ncache roots and deterministic HTTP fixtures; no live metadata sync as an\\nimplicit fixture. Verify shared rendering, layout stability and empty slots.\\n\\nThen record real-browser/real-database integration and section 33 full-page\\ntimings separately for cold browser/cold application cache, cold browser/warm\\napplication cache, and warm browser/warm application cache, including backend\\nrestart and warm-cache upstream-unavailable checks. Record metadata coverage,\\ncache conditions, first/repeat openings, settings, result counts, individual\\ntimings/maxima, browser/backend/upstream request counts and image completion or\\nfailures. Warm application cache must demonstrate zero upstream image requests\\nfor cached entries. Controlled fixtures do not establish live performance.\\nNo measured timing or successful integration is claimed by this decision.\\nDo not conceal pending images, truncate requested results or use lazy loading\\nor forced placeholders to claim the gate is met. Record unavailable-image\\nfallback runs separately from successful delivery and report missing evidence\\nor unmet gates for planner disposition. Request-005 closure and Phase 5 review\\nremain planner-owned; crafting calculations and the active resolution-endpoint\\nstory are unchanged.\\n\\n\"+s[end:],original)
