[20:06:57] def replace_section(s,title,body):
[20:06:57]     pat=r\"(?m)"'^## "+re.escape(title)+r"'"\\n.*?(?="'^## |'"\\Z)\"
[20:06:57]     out,n=re.subn(pat,lambda m:\"## \"+title+\"\\n\\n\"+body+\"\\n\\n\",s,flags=re.S)
[20:06:57]     assert n==1,(title,n)
[20:06:57]     return out
[20:06:57] s=replace_section(s,\"Status\",\"RESOLVED\")
[20:06:57] s=replace_section(s,\"Architect Decision\",\"Class C — architecturally significant technical decision (persistent caching\\nand delivery). Requires Product Owner Decision: NO.\\n\\nSelect a shared source-versioned filesystem cache under ICON_CACHE_DIR,\\nserved through the backend application image endpoint with native browser\\nHTTP caching. TARGET_ARCHITECTURE section 12.1 owns the complete technical\\ncontract; ADR-005 records the rationale and supersedes ADR-004.\\n\\nRequest-005 explicitly authorizes persistent application ownership and rejects\\ndirect external delivery as the normal cold-browser path. Engineering judgment:\\nreusing the existing filesystem root and one desktop/web acquisition adapter\\nmeets that requirement with fewer moving parts than a proxy service or binary\\ndatabase store. Canonical metadata stays in items.icon_url; versioned keys\\nseparate changed URLs, and valid local hits require no ArenaNet request.\\n\\nThe runner-up was serving legacy item-ID files with a source-version sidecar.\\nIt reduces file movement but requires coordinated image/sidecar replacement,\\nstill needs browser versioning, and cannot establish provenance absent from\\nexisting files. Select source-keyed files with conservative legacy adoption\\ninstead. Direct-CDN delivery fails the revised requirement; distributed\\nstorage and external services solve no demonstrated project problem.\\nNo performance measurements or implementation completion are claimed.\")
[20:06:57] s=replace_section(s,\"Resolution\",\"Updated TARGET_ARCHITECTURE section 12.1 with the replacement metadata,\\napplication URL, shared filesystem storage, browser caching, miss/failure,\\nJavaFX migration, retention, deployment persistence and verification contract.\\nCreated ADR-005 and marked ADR-004 superseded while preserving its historical\\nrationale. The earlier architect request was not read or edited.\\n\\nPlanner follow-up remains required: rescope blocked STORY-API-009 and\\nSTORY-WEB-010 before selection, remove their obsolete direct-CDN/no-cache\\nconstraints, and include shared cache/legacy adoption and failure evidence.\\nCarry the persistent-mount constraint into existing deployment scope without\\ncommissioning new deployment work here. Retain roadmap sequencing and the\\nfull-page performance and health-review gates; reconcile planner artifacts as\\nneeded. Request-005 closure and integrated icon-performance assessment remain\\npending. No stories, backlog, roadmap, source, tests or active\\nresolution-endpoint contract were modified.\\n\\nRelevant limitations for follow-up: the observed null-only URL backfill does\\nnot prove metadata coverage/refresh, and legacy item-ID files do not prove\\ntheir source version. These are explicitly addressed by the replacement\\ncontract; real-data verification remains implementation work. No additional\\narchitecture review or User Decision was required.\")
[20:06:57] write(p,s.rstrip()+\"\\n\",original)
[20:06:57] print(\"Updated target contract, ADR-004, ADR-005 and AR-005.\")
